  <prompt>Assemble ALL 11 real trap/invariant probes (tasks 170-180), the 3 real runner ports (tasks 181-183), and the real Ready writer (task 184) into H13E2EAcceptanceGateHandler.cs's FINAL aggregation logic: the gate advances to Completed (and the Ready writer fires) if and ONLY IF every T1-T6 trap, every I1-I5 invariant, the naming-conformance check, and the cost-envelope check ALL genuinely pass -- per this project's spec.md acceptance criteria ('ANY trap OR invariant OR cost fail fails the run', per the existing risk register entry for H13). This task's job is the AGGREGATION LOGIC ITSELF, not any individual probe (those are tasks 170-184) -- verify the existing aggregation-decision code (if any exists as scaffolding) correctly composes the now-real results instead of the previously-uniform InfraFault placeholders.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in multi-check gate-aggregation logic, ensuring a composite Pass requires EVERY constituent check to genuinely pass, with no silent short-circuit or masking.</role>

  <goal>H13E2EAcceptanceGateHandler.cs's aggregation logic correctly composes all 11 probes + 3 runners + the Ready writer: a Completed/Ready outcome requires EVERY constituent check to Pass; ANY single Fail (from any of the 15 checks) produces a non-Ready outcome with a clear, itemized report of WHICH check(s) failed (not merely an aggregate Fail with no detail). A comprehensive test suite exercises every combination of one-check-fails-rest-pass, confirming the aggregation never silently masks a single failure.</goal>

  <context>
